cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its derived alloy candidate data, please cite it as below."
title: "Aloy: A transparent machine-learning pipeline for inverse design of low-cost, high-strength aluminium and magnesium alloys"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Al-Kaysan"
    given-names: "Abdul Afif"
    affiliation: "Institut Teknologi Bandung, Metallurgical Engineering"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-19"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/beduldul/aloy-alloy-design"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22844739"
keywords:
  - materials informatics
  - aluminium alloys
  - magnesium alloys
  - multi-objective optimisation
  - Bayesian optimisation
  - CALPHAD
  - alloy design
abstract: >
  A reproducible pipeline that turns two open experimental alloy datasets into
  Pareto-optimal candidate compositions, with leakage-free cross-validation,
  physics-based (Hume-Rothery) and CALPHAD phase screening, Bayesian active
  learning, and conformal prediction intervals. It produces explicit laboratory
  protocols and benchmarks every recommendation against commercial AA7075,
  AA6061, AZ91D, ZK60 and WE43. Every reported number is accompanied by an error
  bar and every limitation is stated; the package is an experiment-prioritisation
  tool, not a substitute for experiment.
